## Selected live-to-Record instrument

Let

\[
 W_{f,b}=|Locked_{f,b}\rangle\langle Ready_f|,
\qquad
 K_{f,b}=\sqrt{E_b}\otimes W_{f,b}.                       \tag{12}
\]

The six Ready words are orthogonal. If

\[
 P_{\rm ready}=\sum_f|Ready_f\rangle\langle Ready_f|,
\]

then

\[
 \sum_{f,b}K_{f,b}^\dagger K_{f,b}
 =I_{\rm live}\otimes P_{\rm ready}.                      \tag{13}
\]

Adding

\[
 K_{\rm STOP}=I_{\rm live}\otimes(I-P_{\rm ready})        \tag{14}
\]

gives a complete CPTP instrument on the whole 32-qubit block. Because the
Kraus identity (13)--(14) is an operator identity, complete positivity and
trace preservation hold with arbitrary external references, without
allocating a dense `2^32` matrix.

For input `rho` and supplied `Ready_f`, branch `(f,b)` has

\[
 \Pr(b|\rho)=\operatorname{Tr}(\rho E_b),                 \tag{15}
\]

and normalized live poststate

\[
 {\sqrt{E_b}\rho\sqrt{E_b}\over\operatorname{Tr}(\rho E_b)}.
                                                               \tag{16}
\]

The primary executes (15)--(16) for every effect on a correlated six-live-site
two-sector state entangled with an external reference. The branch
probabilities are positive, output norms are one, and unequal sector
