## Complete-M2 QND boundary

Let `{Phi_b}` be arbitrary CP branch maps on the six-qubit input and suppose
their nonselective channel leaves every state exactly unchanged:

\[
 \sum_b\Phi_b=\operatorname{Id}_{M_{64}}.                 \tag{18}
\]

The Choi matrix of the identity channel is the rank-one operator
`|Omega><Omega|`. Each `J(Phi_b)` is positive and their sum is that rank-one
operator, so every branch Choi matrix has the same one-dimensional support:

\[
 J(\Phi_b)=q_b|\Omega\rangle\langle\Omega|,\qquad q_b\ge0.
                                                               \tag{19}
\]

Therefore

\[
 \Phi_b=q_b\operatorname{Id},\qquad
 \Phi_b^*(I)=q_bI.                                       \tag{20}
\]

Every informative Block09 effect is nonconstant, so no instrument with those
effects can satisfy (18). The conclusion is independent of the Lüders choice.

The strengthened primary also executes the required boundary control. A CNOT
copies an arbitrary diagonal two-label Record distribution to a blank pointer
while leaving the old diagonal state unchanged. Applied to a noncommuting
superposition, the same CNOT dephases the old marginal. Thus commuting
orthogonal Record statistics remain a lawful QND route, while complete
arbitrary-`M_2` preservation does not.

